  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "As we all know, the current performance ranking system is not all-encompassing and is meant to serve as a general \"is this optimized?\" checklist. But I've had one growing concern that has seemed to become worse recently. Many avatars have way too many animation layers. It seems to be a rising trend to have at minimum 80 FX layers (I've had to count with the avatar debug); and this is excluding avatar addons which keep increasing in complexity. \n\nI think we need another metric that counts total animation layers, but weighs lightly on the performance rank. \n\nMany avatars go under the guise as a good performing avatar, but are absolute frame time hogs. I think it might encourage more thorough optimization by making users more conscious about what affects performance. There are even easy solutions like VRCFury which can convert simple toggles into a single-layer blendtree.",
